### 17.3 Text Output Format

```
Trend Analysis (<N> reports)
==========================
<step_id>  <classification>  [<s1>, <s2>, ...]  stability=<value>
...
---
<total> steps: <stable> stable, <flaky> flaky, <degrading> degrading, <improving> improving
Overall stability: <pct>%
```

- Each step on one line. Status values are comma-separated. Null entries display as `-`.
- Stability value is formatted to two decimal places (e.g., `0.50`, `1.00`).
- Overall stability percentage is formatted to one decimal place (e.g., `75.0%`, `100.0%`).
- Steps are listed in alphabetical order by `step_id`.
